idence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tina Kotek (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Oregon's governor race pits incumbent Democrat Tina Kotek against Republican Christine Drazan, with independent Brett Smith also on the ballot. Despite the state's Democratic lean, the contest is competitive: recent polls show Kotek ahead by only low single digits, and one September survey had Drazan slightly in front. Kotek's favorability sits at 38 percent, and coverage in the final week describes a neck-and-neck finish.\n\nStill, structural factors favor Kotek. Oregon has not elected a Republican governor since 1982, she carries the advantages of incumbency, and outside groups have poured millions into both campaigns under the state's no-limits donation rules. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean Democratic, with a few saying Likely Democratic, and prediction markets give Kotek roughly an 80 percent chance. The forecast expects a narrow Kotek win, with enough uncertainty that an upset cannot be ruled out.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.91, "margin": 7.23}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7143, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6673, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6685, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7753, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7762, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7967, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7478, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.743, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7131, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7358, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7337, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7182, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7487, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7254, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7322, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7748, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_d